      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woods_Cross%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Woods Cross lies near the bottom of the Great Salt Lake Basin, about eight miles north of Salt Lake City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://onlineutah.us/woodscrossdhistory.shtml"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city of Woods Cross sits along the Wasatch Front next to the Wasatch Mountain Range.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woods_Cross%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mountain springs and snowpack running off the Wasatch Mountains provide the water supply for Woods Cross.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woods_Cross%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early settlers arrived in 1848 and built cellars and dugouts near the banks of the Jordan River in Woods Cross.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://onlineutah.us/woodscrossdhistory.shtml"
    },
    {
